{"qid":"Q157904","names":["Sultanate of Zanzibar"],"title":"Sultanate of Zanzibar","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Sultanate of Zanzibar was established in 1856 when Majid bin Said became sultan following the partition of the Omani Empire between him and his brother Thuwaini, who received Oman. Zanzibar dominated the East African coast's clove trade and served as a hub for ivory and enslaved-people commerce; Britain declared a protectorate over the islands in 1890, and the Anglo-Zanzibar War of 27 August 1896—lasting approximately 38–45 minutes—remains the shortest recorded war in history. The sultanate ended on 12 January 1964 when the Zanzibar Revolution overthrew Sultan Jamshid bin Abdullah; Zanzibar subsequently merged with Tanganyika to form Tanzania.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Island core territory is clear; mainland coastal claims and the extent of effective control at different dates are less precisely documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Sultanate of Zanzibar","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Zanzibar"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Anglo-Zanzibar War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Zanzibar_War"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Zanzibar Revolution","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zanzibar_Revolution"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Majid bin Said","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Majid_bin_Said"}],"britannica":"place/Sultanate-of-Zanzibar","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Sultanate of Zanzibar","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Majid bin Said","nativeName":"ماجد بن سعيد","roman":"Majid bin Said","start":1856,"end":1870,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},